column2:
These point to another copy of LycanZip (or to its old folder): {0}. Opening or right-clicking archives won't use this copy. Use this copy instead?

Now used: {2}
This copy: {1}

The settings and templates are copied to the program folder:
{0}

The files in the old location aren't deleted.

The settings and templates are copied to the user folder:
{0}

The files in the program folder aren't deleted.

The Microsoft Store version of LycanZip is also installed. It provides the right-click menu and the file types, so this copy has switched its own off and File Explorer shows LycanZip only once.

Keeping one copy is simpler: you can remove the one you do not use in Installed apps.

